      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I recognize that multiplying 99 by 99 can be approached by breaking down the numbers to make the calculation easier.\n\nI'll start by expressing 99 as 100 minus 1. This simplifies the multiplication process.\n\nNext, I'll apply the distributive property to multiply 99 by 99. This means I'll multiply 99 by 100 and then subtract 99 from the result.\n\nCalculating 99 times 100 gives me 9900. Then, subtracting 99 from 9900 results in 9801.\n\nTherefore, the product of 99 and 99 is 9801.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 99 and 99?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 99 and 99 step by step.\n\n1. **Break down the numbers for easier multiplication:**\n   \n   We can express 99 as \\(100 - 1\\).\n\n2. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   \n   \\[\n   99 \\times 99 = (100 - 1) \\times 99\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   = 100 \\times 99 - 1 \\times 99\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Calculate each part:**\n   \n   - \\(100 \\times 99 = 9900\\)\n   - \\(1 \\times 99 = 99\\)\n\n4. **Subtract the second result from the first:**\n   \n   \\[\n   9900 - 99 = 9801\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\n\nThe product of 99 and 99 is \\(\\boxed{9801}\\).",
