      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I recognize that both numbers, 97 and 91, are close to 100. This proximity to a round number makes it easier to apply a multiplication strategy that simplifies the calculation.\n\nI'll use the difference of squares formula, which states that (a - b)(a + b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2. Here, I can let a = 90 and b = 7, since 97 = 90 + 7 and 91 = 90 - 7.\n\nApplying the formula:\n(90 + 7)(90 - 7) = 90\u00b2 - 7\u00b2\n\nCalculating each part:\n90\u00b2 = 8100\n7\u00b2 = 49\n\nSubtracting the two results:\n8100 - 49 = 8051\n\nTherefore, the product of 97 and 91 is 8051.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 97 and 91?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of **97** and **91** step by step.\n\n1. **Break down the numbers:**\n   - **97** can be expressed as **100 - 3**.\n   - **91** can be expressed as **100 - 9**.\n\n2. **Apply the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   (100 - 3) \\times (100 - 9) = 100 \\times 100 - 100 \\times 9 - 3 \\times 100 + 3 \\times 9\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each term:**\n   - \\(100 \\times 100 = 10,\\!000\\)\n   - \\(100 \\times 9 = 900\\)\n   - \\(3 \\times 100 = 300\\)\n   - \\(3 \\times 9 = 27\\)\n\n4. **Combine the results:**\n   \\[\n   10,\\!000 - 900 - 300 + 27 = 10,\\!000 - 1,\\!200 + 27 = 8,\\!800 + 27 = 8,\\!827\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of **97** and **91** is \\(\\boxed{8827}\\).",
