      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I recognize that 84 and 86 are both close to 80 and 90, but more precisely, they are near 85. To simplify the multiplication, I can express 84 as 85 minus 1 and 86 as 85 plus 1.\n\nUsing the difference of squares formula, (a - b)(a + b) equals a squared minus b squared. Applying this to 84 and 86, I get (85 - 1)(85 + 1), which simplifies to 85 squared minus 1 squared.\n\nCalculating 85 squared, I know that 85 times 85 is 7225. Then, subtracting 1 squared (which is 1) from 7225 gives me 7224.\n\nTherefore, the product of 84 and 86 is 7224.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 84 and 86?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's calculate the product of 84 and 86 step by step.\n\n1. **Express the numbers in a convenient form:**\n   \n   Notice that 84 and 86 are close to 85. We can express them as:\n   \\[\n   84 = 85 - 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 86 = 85 + 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Apply the difference of squares formula:**\n   \n   The product can be written as:\n   \\[\n   (85 - 1)(85 + 1) = 85^2 - 1^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each term:**\n   \n   - Compute \\(85^2\\):\n     \\[\n     85^2 = 7225\n     \\]\n   - Compute \\(1^2\\):\n     \\[\n     1^2 = 1\n     \\]\n\n4. **Subtract the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   7225 - 1 = 7224\n   \\]\n\n# Answer:\n\nThe product of 84 and 86 is \\(\\boxed{7224}\\).",
